   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n<font face=\"Calibri\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\">\r\n<div>I have a query about the R function &#39;order&#39;. I would like to return the ordering</div>\r\n<div>of sorted items from a vector to a label vector and the R function &#39;order&#39; does this.</div>\r\n<div>I tried to use nimbleRcall to get this working but it gives an error</div>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n<div>This is the code I used:</div>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n<div>order &lt;- nimbleRcall(function(x = double(1)){}, Rfun = &#39;order&#39;,</div>\r\n<div>                    returnType = integer(1))</div>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n<div>and the nimble program code is </div>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n<div>CST&lt;-nimbleCode({</div>\r\n<div>for (i in 1:m){</div>\r\n<div>for (j in 1:J){</div>\r\n<div>y0[i,j]~dpois(expe[i,j]*lam0[i,j])</div>\r\n<div>log(lam0[i,j])&lt;-a0+b0[1]*x1[i]+b0[2]*x2[i]</div>\r\n<div>}}</div>\r\n<div>for(i in 1:m){</div>\r\n<div>for(j in 1:J){</div>\r\n<div>for(l in 1:m){</div>\r\n<div>z0[i,j,l]&lt;-2*exp(-abs(lam0[i,j]-lam0[l,j]))/(1+exp(-abs(lam0[i,j]-lam0[l,j])))}</div>\r\n<div>as[1:m]&lt;-z0[i,j,1:m]</div>\r\n<div>C[1:m]&lt;-order(as)</div>\r\n<div>ylab[i,j]&lt;-C[m]</div>\r\n<div>}}</div>\r\n<div>})</div>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n<div>This gives the following error when using nimbleModel:</div>\r\n<div>defining model...</div>\r\n<div>Error in getSymbolicParentNodesRecurse(code, constNames, indexNames, nimbleFunctionNames,  : </div>\r\n<div>  R function &#39;order&#39; has arguments that cannot be evaluated; either the function must be a nimbleFunction or values for the following inputs must be specified as constants in the model: as.</div>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n<div>Any help appreciated</div>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n<div>Andrew</div>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n</span></font>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
