   "subject": "Re: A query about 'order'",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">To give a quick reply, have you tried using a different name for &quot;order&quot;?  Unfortunately, sometimes nimble doesn&#39;t always find things as you would hope based on R&#39;s scoping, and it may be finding R&#39;s order instead of the order you created.  Giving a unique name might help.  Also I think you will need <span style=\"font-family:Calibri;font-size:14.6667px\">C[1:m]&lt;-order(as[1:m]), that is with indices for as.</span><div><span style=\"font-family:Calibri;font-size:14.6667px\"><br></span></div><div><font face=\"Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:14.6667px\">-Perry</span></font></div><div><font face=\"Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:14.6667px\"><br></span></font></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
