     "<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>To give a quick reply, have you tried using a different name for &quot;order&quot;?  Unfortunately, sometimes nimble doesn&#39;t always find things as you would hope based on R&#39;s scoping, and it\r\n may be finding R&#39;s order instead of the order you created.  Giving a unique name might help.  Also I think you will need </span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">C[1:m]&lt;-order(as[1:m]),\r\n that is with indices for as.</span><span>\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">-Perry</span><span><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>On Wed, Aug 14, 2019 at 12:37 PM Lawson, Andrew B. &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">laws...@musc.edu</a>&gt; wrote:<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border:none;border-left:solid #cccccc 1.0pt;padding:0in 0in 0in 6.0pt;margin-left:4.8pt;margin-right:0in\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">I have a query about the R function &#39;order&#39;. I would like to return the ordering<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">of sorted items from a vector to a label vector and the R function &#39;order&#39; does this.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">I tried to use nimbleRcall to get this working but it gives an error<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">This is the code I used:<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">order &lt;- nimbleRcall(function(x = double(1)){}, Rfun = &#39;order&#39;,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">                    returnType = integer(1))<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">and the nimble program code is\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">CST&lt;-nimbleCode({<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">for (i in 1:m){<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">for (j in 1:J){<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri